(781190, 85323, 14355, '<td valign="top">For a newspaper challenge your title sets a confusing stage.  I associate clippings on a wall exactly like this with obsessive behavior found in many movies....... a police detective related title or soemthing about catching a criminal wold have fit this picture like a glove.  And it is a great picture - especially how the darkness on the right is countered by the brightness on the left.   Very nice picture.</td>', 'For a newspaper challenge your title sets a confusing stage.  I associate clippings on a wall exactly like this with obsessive behavior found in many movies....... a police detective related title or soemthing about catching a criminal wold have fit this picture like a glove.  And it is a great picture - especially how the darkness on the right is countered by the brightness on the left.   Very nice picture.', '2004-06-27 03:02:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(781193, 85011, 14355, '<td valign="top">Great picture and title for this challenge.  Considering this is a newspaper challenge -  a little noise from a higher ISO setting would have helped give it the newspaper look, and, allowed for an increase of shutter speed so the arms, face and body would be in near perfect focus while the arms scarf and legs still blured to show motion.   With that said, this is still a GREAT shot because you caught her in the perfect pose.  Excellent work.</td>', 'Great picture and title for this challenge.  Considering this is a newspaper challenge -  a little noise from a higher ISO setting would have helped give it the newspaper look, and, allowed for an increase of shutter speed so the arms, face and body would be in near perfect focus while the arms scarf and legs still blured to show motion.   With that said, this is still a GREAT shot because you caught her in the perfect pose.  Excellent work.', '2004-06-27 03:08:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(781195, 85075, 14355, '<td valign="top">The title and picture match each other perfectly.  However, the double lens flare from the sun and water, plus the flare on the person''s face wold get most newspaper photographers fired.  If you had desaturated the pic it would have helped allot.  Now, the grass sticking out the guy''s ear........... if this is what pictures in the local newspaper of your town look like....... start sending them to Jay Leno.  You''ll make a fortune!  A very funny shot!</td>', 'The title and picture match each other perfectly.  However, the double lens flare from the sun and water, plus the flare on the person''s face wold get most newspaper photographers fired.  If you had desaturated the pic it would have helped allot.  Now, the grass sticking out the guy''s ear........... if this is what pictures in the local newspaper of your town look like....... start sending them to Jay Leno.  You''ll make a fortune!  A very funny shot!', '2004-06-27 03:16:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(781196, 85250, 14355, '<td valign="top">LOL  Great picture and original title.  Nice touch with the desaturation.  Me, I would have used, "Got Milk?".</td>', 'LOL  Great picture and original title.  Nice touch with the desaturation.  Me, I would have used, "Got Milk?".', '2004-06-27 03:19:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(781205, 84585, 4767, '<td valign="top">Wow!   A cogent, convincing, coherent arguement that ends all debate.   Very classy indeed.  Shouldn''t these guys be out washing people''s car windows at some intersection somewhere?<br/> <br/>Technically, a little contrasty for my liking, however, news photos happen when they happen and there''s little control the photog has as to time of day, lighting, etc.</td>', 'Wow!   A cogent, convincing, coherent arguement that ends all debate.   Very classy indeed.  Shouldn''t these guys be out washing people''s car windows at some intersection somewhere? Technically, a little contrasty for my liking, however, news photos happen when they happen and there''s little control the photog has as to time of day, lighting, etc.', '2004-06-27 03:45:44.000000', NULL, 1),
