(786720, 85140, 19608, '<td valign="top">Colorado and many of the surrounding states are in a drought period that is worse than recorded history.  I was only there 4 days and it rained on all four.  I don''t know about newspapers but can tell you it was big news on the local tv stations.</td>', 'Colorado and many of the surrounding states are in a drought period that is worse than recorded history.  I was only there 4 days and it rained on all four.  I don''t know about newspapers but can tell you it was big news on the local tv stations.', '2004-06-30 10:42:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(786736, 85212, 11220, '<td valign="top">This was by far the best photograph in the challenge. I am glad it ribboned, but it should have won. The intensity of the subject combined with the lighting and the contrast were unmatched by anyone else who submitted a photo. Amazing work. I look forward to seeing more from you in the future.</td>', 'This was by far the best photograph in the challenge. I am glad it ribboned, but it should have won. The intensity of the subject combined with the lighting and the contrast were unmatched by anyone else who submitted a photo. Amazing work. I look forward to seeing more from you in the future.', '2004-06-30 10:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(786786, 85268, 4500, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the votes and comments :)<br/> <br/>Most comments were about not making detailed shot of the disaster. <br/>1. it was not disaster and if I''d made a detail, you would see that. <br/>2. I tried a cropped version of this, but the whole sky is probably what makes the picture (I like how the burning sky fades).<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Glacierwolf:</b></div><hr/><i> The six point filter has a nice touch.  The picture looks about 2.5 degrees off to the left...</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I did not use any filter, it is just normal effect from the aperture of the lens. (I used f 8) And the picture is straight, I rotated it according to the chimney in the middle, it is just a curve of the river (I was on bridge over the river).<br/></td>', 'Thank you all for the votes and comments :) Most comments were about not making detailed shot of the disaster. 1. it was not disaster and if I''d made a detail, you would see that. 2. I tried a cropped version of this, but the whole sky is probably what makes the picture (I like how the burning sky fades). Originally posted by Glacierwolf: The six point filter has a nice touch.  The picture looks about 2.5 degrees off to the left... I did not use any filter, it is just normal effect from the aperture of the lens. (I used f 8) And the picture is straight, I rotated it according to the chimney in the middle, it is just a curve of the river (I was on bridge over the river).', '2004-06-30 11:05:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(786839, 85338, 14986, '<td valign="top">~sigh~  We (Cincinnati Reds) are in desperate need of a "real" closer.   Think you could ship him over here?   By the way...nice shot.  I''ve never been able to get one this close.  This really looks like it could be on the sports section of the newspaper.</td>', '~sigh~  We (Cincinnati Reds) are in desperate need of a "real" closer.   Think you could ship him over here?   By the way...nice shot.  I''ve never been able to get one this close.  This really looks like it could be on the sports section of the newspaper.', '2004-06-30 11:29:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(786844, 84064, 200, '<td valign="top">interesting. I gave you the 10...becuase the whole package of this made me smile. Clever and cute. Ahhh..and now I see you''ve added more...the story behind the photo? The scary part is that I get it. Whatever the soul tortured angst that exists in you...it exists in me too. You have written it out very well. I can not express as well through word...so im hoping to do it with photography. Good luck....<br/></td>', 'interesting. I gave you the 10...becuase the whole package of this made me smile. Clever and cute. Ahhh..and now I see you''ve added more...the story behind the photo? The scary part is that I get it. Whatever the soul tortured angst that exists in you...it exists in me too. You have written it out very well. I can not express as well through word...so im hoping to do it with photography. Good luck....', '2004-06-30 11:32:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(786888, 85234, 6202, '<td valign="top">I am really amazed that only one person caught my misspelling.  I didn''t catch it til after the challenge started and I just left it go.  I''m now punishing myself for it... D-E-M-O-L-I-T-I-O-N!!!!!!</td>', 'I am really amazed that only one person caught my misspelling.  I didn''t catch it til after the challenge started and I just left it go.  I''m now punishing myself for it... D-E-M-O-L-I-T-I-O-N!!!!!!', '2004-06-30 11:57:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(786902, 84636, 6521, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for great comments and support.<br/> <br/>I just missed Thorey little bit out of the frame (on the top) when i took this picture, that´s way i used so tight crop. I really don´t see that as a problem, as a matter of fact i thought it was very cool. That´s why i used this one but not some other picture from that day.<br/> <br/>I thought it was a good idea at the time to use border. To day i don´t think it was such a good idea after all but there is nothing i can do about it now, right?<br/> <br/>Again, thanks alot!!</td>', 'Thank you all for great comments and support. I just missed Thorey little bit out of the frame (on the top) when i took this picture, that´s way i used so tight crop. I really don´t see that as a problem, as a matter of fact i thought it was very cool. That´s why i used this one but not some other picture from that day. I thought it was a good idea at the time to use border. To day i don´t think it was such a good idea after all but there is nothing i can do about it now, right? Again, thanks alot!!', '2004-06-30 12:03:39.000000', NULL, 0),
